# x86 Shadow Features — Emit Module Audit
//
File: openOODA/audit/x86-shadow-features.oot
// Status: open — produced 2026-08-25 from x86 deep-dive
//
// Logline: Maps every x86_emit_*.oo and x86_ssa_emit_*.oo public fn to its shape guard and finds pairs that compete for the same source input.
//
// Setup: Read every emit module under ooda/oodac/, cross-referenced trigger tokens and body-shape predicates against the dispatch ladder in ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo:73-196. The typed-AST path (x86_emit_stream_typed) is treated as a separate backend layer, not a shadow of the token path.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Inventory 38 emit modules with one-line guard summaries.
//   2. List 12 shadow pairs where two modules accept the same source input.
//   3. Decide KEEP BOTH, MERGE, or DELETE per pair.
//   4. Count lines saved if all DELETEs happen.
//
// residual: AArch64 audit stays later; the typed-AST path is treated as a parallel layer, not a shadow.

---

